* Common-emitter amplifier example (demonstrates .subckt subcircuits)
* Custom SPICE-style netlist. Comment lines start with '*'; inline comments follow ';'.

.title Common-Emitter Amplifier

* BJT model: NPN, simplified Ebers-Moll (IS = saturation current, BF = forward gain, BR = reverse gain)
.model QNPN npn(bf=150 br=5 is=2e-15)

* Subcircuit definition: common-emitter stage, port order is in out vcc gnd
.subckt ceamp in out vcc gnd
Cin  in   base  1u      ; input coupling capacitor
R1   vcc  base  27k     ; upper bias resistor
R2   base gnd   3.9k    ; lower bias resistor
RC   vcc  col   2.2k    ; collector load resistor
RE   em   gnd   820     ; emitter resistor (sets the operating point)
CE   em   gnd   100u    ; emitter bypass capacitor (boosts AC gain)
Cout col  out   1u      ; output coupling capacitor
RL   out  gnd   10k     ; load resistor
Q1   col  base  em  QNPN
.ends

* Top-level stimulus
VCC  vcc  0  12
Vin  in   0  sin(0 0.01 1k)      ; input: 1 kHz / 10 mV sine wave
X1   in out vcc 0 ceamp          ; subcircuit instance (pin order matches ports)

* Analysis directives
.op
.tran 1e-5 0.005                  ; step 10 us, stop 5 ms

.end